From 3fafc5195f9896e8d26c889efc326d08e3ac4a7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add universal Team hierarchy tab to Team & Access
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Redesigns Team & Access into two tabs per Sumaksh's feedback: "My team"
and "Dealer access". "My team" is new and universal — unlike grant/
revoke (which stays restricted to Senior Sales Associate/Senior Sales
Executive), any active staff member can see a collapsible org-chart of
their own downline (direct + indirect reports_to chain) and drill into
a profile for anyone in it: their dealers (owner + granted-access
combined), total dues across those dealers, order count, and item-wise
sales, all for a chosen period (this month/last month/this quarter).
Targets/performance intentionally left out of this pass per Sumaksh's
call to skip that for now.

New SECURITY DEFINER RPCs, all gated by a new _is_in_my_downline()
check so nobody can see sideways or upward — only their own subtree:
get_my_team_subtree (the tree itself, no role gate), get_team_member_
summary (dues total + dealer count), get_team_member_dealers (owner +
granted list with per-dealer outstanding), get_team_member_orders_
count, get_team_member_item_sales (qty + % share for a date range).
Dues/outstanding reuses the same dealer_ledger balance formula already
used everywhere else in this file; item-wise sales groups order_items
by its existing name snapshot column, no new join needed.

The "Team & Access" entry point on the Sales Dashboard was gated to
senior roles only — removed that gate since My team is now for everyone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
